<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gimry</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gimry is an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avars">Avar</a> village in the mountains of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dagestan">Dagestan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, the birthplace of both <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghazi-muhammad">Ghazi Muhammad</a>, the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">imam</a> of the Caucasian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imamate">Imamate</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam-shamil">Imam Shamil</a>. In 1832 Russian troops stormed it; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghazi">Ghazi</a> Muhammad was killed defending it, while the wounded Shamil escaped.</p></div>
